    "created_at": "2016-11-01T20:22:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-01T20:22:18Z",
    "body": "Fascinating. I cannot find anything on how to enable spatial navigation in Chrome, but some Googling shows it might be enable-able in Opera?\n\nI'm not sure what we should do with this exactly. Maybe we should say something like\n\n> The user agent should <ins>provide a mode which allows</ins> the user to manually trigger elements that have an activation behavior, for instance using keyboard or voice input, or through mouse clicks. <ins>In this mode,</ins> when the user triggers an element with a defined activation behavior in a manner other than clicking it, the default action of the interaction event must be to fire a click event at the element.\n> \n> <ins>NOTE: such a mode cannot be turned on by default, as many pages add key event listeners in addition to click event listeners, and so turning it on results in both events being dispatched.</ins>\n\nThen we'd update the note in @patrickhlauke's original PR to talk about firing the click event in this mode only.\n\n---\n\nOr, we could just remove it entirely, and leave this spatial navigation mode as some sort of outside-the-spec enhancement?\n\n@smaug----, do you know if Firefox has any mode like this? Maybe when a11y technology is enabled?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
